Auditable trait: ensure not logging during audit insert itself. Use app(AuditLogger::class)->record.

Filter sensitive attributes: exclude password, remember_token, nik_hash, updated_at maybe no. Provide `auditExcluded` property default ['password','remember_token','nik_hash'].

AuditLogger:
```php
class AuditLogger {
 public function record(string $event, Model $model, ?array $old = null, ?array $new = null): void
 {
   $request = request();
   DB::table('audit_logs')->insert([...created_at=>now()]);
 }
 public function recordRaw(string $event, string $type, ?int $id, array $old=[], array $new=[])...
}
```
Avoid events on AuditLog itself (not Auditable so fine).

For updated event: getChanges() keys; old values from getOriginal($key) but getOriginal returns raw (encrypted for casts). Need raw DB values? For audit, we want original stored? For encrypted, raw ciphertext would leak meaningless. Use `$model->getOriginal()` and then maybe we should use getRawOriginal for all. Hmm. Use getOriginal which applies casts? Actually getOriginal returns cast values through attribute casting? getOriginal($key) returns original attributes (raw) unless cast? In Laravel, getOriginal applies casts via transformModelValue in newer versions. I think `getOriginal()` returns raw values with casts applied since 9? There's getRawOriginal. I'll use getOriginal and then only include changed keys; then run through a sanitizer that removes excluded keys.

Potential problem: encrypted cast values in old array are decrypted fine. Good. But inserting encrypted NIK into audit_logs old/new JSON would store plaintext NIK — sensitive! Better exclude 'nik','account_number','npwp','bpjs_kesehatan_no','bpjs_tk_no' from audit values and instead record `nik` masked? For employee, audit should record changes but mask sensitive. Add masking: for keys in sensitive list, set '[disembunyikan]' if value present. Audit log still records that it changed.

Implement AuditLogger::sanitize(array $values): remove password/remember_token, mask nik etc.

Trait:
```php
trait Auditable {
 public static function bootAuditable(): void {
   static::created(function (Model $model) { app(AuditLogger::class)->record('create', $model, null, $model->getAttributes()); });
   static::updated(function (Model $model) { $changed = $model->getChanges(); unset($changed['updated_at']); $old=[]; foreach(array_keys($changed) as $k){$old[$k]=$model->getOriginal($k);} app(...)->record('update',$model,$old,$changed); });
   static::deleted(...);
 }
}
```
But `getAttributes()` returns raw encrypted values -> then sanitize masks sensitive keys; fine. But raw for other encrypted fields masked. For created, include all attributes except excluded; DB raw values for booleans/dates are strings, acceptable. Better use $model->attributesToArray() which applies casts and hides hidden. Use that.

For created: new = attributesToArray (hides password? User not auditable anyway).

NumberSequenceService:
```php
public function next(string $code, ?CarbonInterface $at = null): string
{
  $at = $at ? Carbon::instance(...) : now('Asia/Jakarta');
  return DB::transaction(function() use(...) {
    $seq = DB::table('number_sequences')->where('code',$code)->lockForUpdate()->first();
    if(!$seq) throw new RuntimeException("...");
    $next = (int)$seq->next_number;
    $lastReset = $seq->last_reset_at ? Carbon::parse($seq->last_reset_at) : null;
    $reset = false;
    if ($seq->reset_period==='yearly' && (!$lastReset || $lastReset->year !== $at->year)) { $next=1; $reset=true; }
    if monthly && (!$lastReset || $lastReset->format('Y-m') !== $at->format('Y-m')) { $next=1; $reset=true; }
    $formatted = $this->format($seq->pattern, $seq->prefix, $next, $at);
    DB::table(...)->update(['next_number'=>$next+1,'last_reset_at'=>$reset?$at->toDateString():$seq->last_reset_at,'updated_at'=>now()]);
    return $formatted;
  });
}
format: replace {prefix}, {year}, {month}, {seq:N} or {seq}, {roman}? Keep simple; support {seq:4}.
```
Pattern `{prefix}-{year}-{seq:4}`.

